# Build-context hygiene for the root Dockerfile. The image build only needs the
# Go module sources plus go.mod/go.sum; everything below is either large,
# secret, host-only, or actively breaks the build, so it is kept out of the
# context COPY . . sends to the daemon.

# Git metadata — large and never needed inside the build (the VERSION stamp is
# passed as a --build-arg, not read from .git).
.git

# Gitignored reference trees: cauldron/ pulls external deps the root module
# lacks, so its presence breaks `go build ./...` (see learnings: cauldron breaks
# a fresh build).
cauldron/

# Compiled monitor binaries — the 26MB artifacts `go build` emits at the repo
# root and the command dir; the image builds its own, never copies the host's.
/iscc-monitor
/cmd/iscc-monitor/iscc-monitor

# Local SQLite databases and WAL/SHM sidecars — runtime state, never source. The
# `*.db`/`*.sqlite*` globs do NOT match the `-wal`/`-shm` sidecars, so list those
# explicitly. (.claude/settings.local.json is already covered by the .claude/ line.)
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite*
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Local secrets — never bake a developer's credentials into the build-STAGE layer.
# The published image is unaffected (the final stage only COPY --from=build's the
# binary), but a `.dockerignore` for a `COPY . .` Dockerfile must be a SUPERSET of
# the repo .gitignore's never-commit secret set, as defense-in-depth hygiene.
.env
.env.*
**/auth.json

# Loop/agent and host-only trees that are irrelevant to the build.
.claude/
.devcontainer/
.github/
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
